{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377191807,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c937109b001RiRDqBg2H7dtT5","messageID":"msg_1c936ff5f001xxn8FaNQiX7x8y","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>Let me check the environment: Python version, node version, whether npm/pip work, network access.\n\nLet me plan the tasks.\n\nKey considerations:\n- Backend: Flask, SQLite under ./data, token auth (Bearer token), track CRUD, plays increment.\n- Frontend: React + TS + Vite + Tailwind CSS. Tailwind v4 has a Vite plugin (`@tailwindcss/vite`). But network availability: \"The sandbox can install packages from the public package registries (through a read-only cache)\". So npm install should work. But the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` with the existing package-lock.json — I'll need to update package-lock.json with new deps (tailwindcss, @tailwindcss/vite). Let me check if npm install works in the sandbox.\n\nLet me check environment first.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377191579,"end":1794377191800}}}
