{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377202242,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c9373a1a001lqcDdRpgOIbTnN","messageID":"msg_1c9372a17001grZ5L7UjVeS5fY","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>The npm install dry run said \"up to date\" — odd; it didn't actually install tailwindcss. Let me check npm registry access properly.\n\nAlso pip download in /tmp/opencode was denied by permission rules? Interesting - it says external_directory deny for *. Hmm, /tmp/opencode/piptest — allowed pattern is /tmp/opencode/*. Maybe the subdirectory pattern. Let me just try pip install in workspace instead.\n\nLet me check if pip has flask already installed.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377202202,"end":1794377202237}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794377203060,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_9Sy38C4pra241pPx0FJqu0pX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"import flask; print(flask.__version__)\"; pip list 2>/dev/null | head -30"},"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask; print(flask.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\nPackage   Version\n--------- -------\npackaging 25.0\npip       25.1.1\nwheel     0.46.1\n","metadata":{"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask; print(flask.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\nPackage   Version\n--------- -------\npackaging 25.0\npip       25.1.1\nwheel     0.46.1\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"import flask; print(flask.__version__)\"; pip list 2>/dev/null | head -30","time":{"start":1794377202213,"end":1794377203056}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c9373a1e001AjeVPJ4CnNLo4S","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","messageID":"msg_1c9372a17001grZ5L7UjVeS5fY"}}
