{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377342937,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c9395fc0001OCR0gyZ3Zw1vbh","messageID":"msg_1c93949a4001edBZme8sw3vp23","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>The /tmp/opencode path is being denied (maybe because of the rm -rf or the DATA_DIR assignment?). Let me just use a data dir inside /workspace (e.g. /workspace/data, which is gitignored? .dockerignore excludes data/*.db). Let me check .gitignore — there is none in the repo listing. `git status` showed clean with no data dir. The .dockerignore ignores data/*.db. I should add data/ to .gitignore maybe. Let me check if there's a .gitignore.\n\nI'll use the default data dir /workspace/data for tests, and clean up afterwards (or leave it; it's the runtime data dir, harmless but let's remove the db at the end).</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377342912,"end":1794377342932}}}
