{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377382647,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c939fae0001snPRFfpkfTcQvF","messageID":"msg_1c939e2cb001xj3knIgHltHWxn","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>The other deps use exact versions (no caret). Let me pin tailwindcss and @tailwindcss/vite exactly to match the style of the existing file: \"tailwindcss\": \"4.3.5\", \"@tailwindcss/vite\": \"4.3.5\".\n\nThen run npm install to sync the lock file.\n\nAlso I should add TypeScript dev deps? The project uses .tsx but has no typescript dependency?! Let me check: package.json has react, react-dom, @vitejs/plugin-react, vite — no typescript. The build works because Vite/esbuild strips types without type-checking. But for a proper TS project, I should add typescript and @types/react, @types/react-dom. The README says \"The frontend is a Vite project (React + TypeScript)\". The existing setup lacks typescript. Adding typescript + types is good for a typecheck script. Let me add them (dev deps) and a `typecheck` script.\n\nVersions: typescript latest (5.x), @types/react ^19, @types/react-dom ^19. Let me install and pin.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377382624,"end":1794377382642}}}
