{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377611932,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c93d7a840016EKYZKCTcozeNS","messageID":"msg_1c93d6915001L1rh2EX9kWyu6t","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>`npm ci` works with the updated lock file.\n\nNow let's run the whole stack and test with curl. I'll start gunicorn on port 8000 with the data dir at /workspace/data.\n\nNote: the Dockerfile runs gunicorn with `--pythonpath backend app:app` from /app. Let me replicate locally:\n\ncd /workspace && .venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n\nThen curl the endpoints.\n\nBut careful: the data dir at /workspace/data would be created. I'll clean it up at the end.\n\nLet's also double check that `data` should be gitignored. There's no .gitignore in the repo. The .dockerignore excludes data/*.db. I'll add a .gitignore with data/ and node_modules etc. Let me check git status to see if the data dir would be committed. Adding a .gitignore is a sensible addition.\n\nLet me start the server and test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377611908,"end":1794377611928}}}
