{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377695930,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c93ec2aa001Xm02P1r5hru2XQ","messageID":"msg_1c93e9d380017GnxRAfSPSWAo7","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>The app renders. The user isn't signed in because my `localStorage.setItem` happens before the bundle evaluates... wait, the auth provider reads the token on mount → `api.me()` is called (I see \"GET /api/auth/me\" in the calls) but the state.token in my stub is null (my stub's `state.token` variable is separate from localStorage). The stub returned 401 because `state.token` was null → the app cleared the token and showed the guest view.\n\nLet me fix the stub: initialize state.token = \"tok-login\" and state.user = {id: 2, username: \"signedin_user\"}.\n\nLet me re-run with that fix.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377695914,"end":1794377695927}}}
