{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794377744292,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c93f7f840014OY7ibAlFXU3bj","messageID":"msg_1c93f5305001yk5eT8DbmPkdDj","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377744293,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c93f7f870011SfIgH08gyJG9w","messageID":"msg_1c93f5305001yk5eT8DbmPkdDj","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>The form submission didn't work. Possibly the submit event isn't triggering React's onSubmit because React 19 attaches the event listener to the root container and the form's submit event bubbles... it should work.\n\nHmm, but jsdom's form submission: dispatching a \"submit\" event manually should trigger React's handler (React listens for \"submit\" on the root).\n\nWait — the issue might be that `doc.querySelector(\"#track-title\").form` returns the form element, and my submit dispatch works, but React's synthetic event system requires the event to be trusted? No, React handles dispatched events fine.\n\nAnother possibility: `setInput` didn't update React's state because React 19 uses a different value setter detection. The standard trick works with React's `input` event. Hmm, but for React 19, the recommended approach is `el.value = value` + dispatch \"input\" — the native setter trick is needed because React tracks the value. Let me verify: React's `restoreControlledState` uses a value tracker; setting `el.value` directly updates the tracker, so React thinks nothing changed and skips the onChange. Using the native prototype setter avoids updating React's tracker... Actually the tracker is installed on the node instance (`node._valueTracker`), and it overrides the `value` property on the *instance*. So calling the prototype setter directly bypasses the instance-level override → the tracker's lastValue stays stale → React detects the change. That's the standard trick and should work.\n\nBut wait: my `setInput` uses `Object.getPrototypeOf(el)` → for an input element that's HTMLInputElement.prototype → the \"value\" descriptor exists → good.\n\nSo why didn't the form submit? Let me debug: maybe the form's submit handler was called but `api.createTrack` failed and the error is displayed... but \"shows API validation message\" failed too.\n\nHmm, maybe the submit event isn't reaching React. In React 19, the root container is #root, and the form is inside it. Dispatching a \"submit\" event on the form with bubbles: true should propagate to #root and React's delegated listener should fire.\n\nUnless... React 19 attaches listeners to the container but for \"submit\" events, React uses the non-delegated approach? No, submit is delegated.\n\nLet me debug by adding a console log in the test: check whether the input values are actually set in React state (i.e., whether the component re-rendered). Let me test with a simple check: after setInput, read the value from the DOM and check if the component state updated (e.g. the button's disabled state).\n\nActually — a simpler explanation: `window.eval(code)` runs the bundle in the jsdom window context. The React event system might be attaching to `document` of the jsdom — that's the same document. Hmm.\n\nLet me debug step by step: add a listener on the form for \"submit\" to see if the event is dispatched, and check whether the React state updated by looking at some DOM change.\n\nLet me write a quick debug script.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377744263,"end":1794377744287}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794377745735,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_7ihWsi7PZMQfSZ0k2hdNphJX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/.run/jsdomtest && cat > debug.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { JSDOM, VirtualConsole } from \"jsdom\";\n\nconst DIST = \"/workspace/frontend/dist\";\nconst html = fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"index.html\"), \"utf8\");\nconst virtualConsole = new VirtualConsole();\nvirtualConsole.on(\"jsdomError\", (e) => console.log(\"JSDOM ERROR:\", e.message));\nvirtualConsole.on(\"error\", (...args) => console.log(\"console.error:\", ...args));\nconst dom = new JSDOM(html, { runScripts: \"outside-only\", pretendToBeVisual: true, url: \"http://localhost:8000/\", virtualConsole });\nconst { window } = dom;\nwindow.fetch = async () => ({ ok: true, status: 200, text: async () => JSON.stringify({ items: [], total: 0, page: 1, page_size: 10 }) });\nwindow.localStorage.setItem(\"audio-library.token\", \"tok\");\nfor (const file of fs.readdirSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\")).filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".js\"))) {\n  window.eval(fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\", file), \"utf8\"));\n}\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nawait sleep(200);\nconst doc = window.document;\nconst input = doc.querySelector(\"#track-title\");\nconsole.log(\"input found:\", !!input);\nconst proto = Object.getPrototypeOf(input);\nconst setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(proto, \"value\").set;\nsetter.call(input, \"Hello\");\ninput.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\nawait sleep(100);\nconsole.log(\"input value after event:\", input.value);\nconst form = input.form;\nconsole.log(\"form found:\", !!form);\nform.addEventListener(\"submit\", () => console.log(\"native submit listener fired\"));\nform.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"submit\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\nawait sleep(200);\nconsole.log(\"body text:\", doc.body.textContent.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").slice(0, 200));\nEOF\ntimeout 120 node debug.mjs 2>&1 | tail -20"},"output":"input found: true\ninput value after event: Hello\nform found: true\nnative submit listener fired\nbody text:  Audio LibraryStream tracks stored as linksSigned in as Sign outAdd a trackTracks are stored as links to audio files — the library never uploads or stores audio.TitleArtistAudio URLOnly http and https\n","metadata":{"output":"input found: true\ninput value after event: Hello\nform found: true\nnative submit listener fired\nbody text:  Audio LibraryStream tracks stored as linksSigned in as Sign outAdd a trackTracks are stored as links to audio files — the library never uploads or stores audio.TitleArtistAudio URLOnly http and https\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/.run/jsdomtest && cat > debug.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { JSDOM, VirtualConsole } from \"jsdom\";\n\nconst DIST = \"/workspace/frontend/dist\";\nconst html = fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"index.html\"), \"utf8\");\nconst virtualConsole = new VirtualConsole();\nvirtualConsole.on(\"jsdomError\", (e) => console.log(\"JSDOM ERROR:\", e.message));\nvirtualConsole.on(\"error\", (...args) => console.log(\"console.error:\", ...args));\nconst dom = new JSDOM(html, { runScripts: \"outside-only\", pretendToBeVisual: true, url: \"http://localhost:8000/\", virtualConsole });\nconst { window } = dom;\nwindow.fetch = async () => ({ ok: true, status: 200, text: async () => JSON.stringify({ items: [], total: 0, page: 1, page_size: 10 }) });\nwindow.localStorage.setItem(\"audio-library.token\", \"tok\");\nfor (const file of fs.readdirSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\")).filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".js\"))) {\n  window.eval(fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\", file), \"utf8\"));\n}\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nawait sleep(200);\nconst doc = window.document;\nconst input = doc.querySelector(\"#track-title\");\nconsole.log(\"input found:\", !!input);\nconst proto = Object.getPrototypeOf(input);\nconst setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(proto, \"value\").set;\nsetter.call(input, \"Hello\");\ninput.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\nawait sleep(100);\nconsole.log(\"input value after event:\", input.value);\nconst form = input.form;\nconsole.log(\"form found:\", !!form);\nform.addEventListener(\"submit\", () => console.log(\"native submit listener fired\"));\nform.dispatchEvent(new window.Event(\"submit\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\nawait sleep(200);\nconsole.log(\"body text:\", doc.body.textContent.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").slice(0, 200));\nEOF\ntimeout 120 node debug.mjs 2>&1 | tail -20","time":{"start":1794377744275,"end":1794377745714}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c93f7f8b001lqh1PASsOjouXO","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","messageID":"msg_1c93f5305001yk5eT8DbmPkdDj"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794377745735,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c93f8535001Hjlr2L57mnPB8I","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_1c93f5305001yk5eT8DbmPkdDj","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":68571,"input":204,"output":516,"reasoning":631,"cache":{"write":0,"read":67220}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794377757672,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c93fb396001Vlv5FZzJSviayy","messageID":"msg_1c93f85420013uLPE0XXZ30uX1","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794377757673,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"id":"prt_1c93fb3cc001qk6I2b47nASUoL","messageID":"msg_1c93f85420013uLPE0XXZ30uX1","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","type":"text","text":"<think>The submit event fires natively but React's handler doesn't run (no API call, no state change). The input value was set but React state may not have updated either.\n\nWhy? React 19 attaches its event listeners to the root container when using createRoot. The `submit` event bubbles from the form to #root → React should handle it.\n\nHmm, wait. There's a known issue: React's event delegation requires the event to be dispatched on an element inside the container — which is the case.\n\nLet me check whether React's onChange fired for the input: if the state didn't update, then submitting would send empty fields. But we saw no fetch to /api/tracks at all, so onSubmit didn't fire.\n\nMaybe the issue is that `window.eval()` executes the code in the window context but the bundled React attaches listeners using the `document` from the module scope — that's the same window.document. Should be fine.\n\nHmm, another thought: React's event system uses \"pointer\" events for some interactions but submit is a discrete event handled via the root container listener... Let me check if React 19 uses `addEventListener` on the container for all events. Yes.\n\nWait — maybe the issue is the jsdom `Event` constructor: `new window.Event(\"submit\", {bubbles: true, cancelable: true})` creates a generic Event, not an HTMLFormEvent. React doesn't care about the interface, it just reads the type and target.\n\nHmm, but React's `SyntheticEvent` for submit requires `event.target` to be a form for `onSubmit`... it is.\n\nLet me test if a simple React onClick works in this jsdom setup (the play button click). In the interaction test, the click on the delete button did nothing either (the error was that `doc.querySelector('button[aria-label^=\"Delete\"]')` was null — no tracks existed because the add failed).\n\nSo maybe NO React event handlers work in this jsdom setup. Let me test a click on the \"Sign out\" button and see if localStorage is cleared / the header changes.\n\nActually — I bet the issue is this: React 19's `createRoot` attaches listeners to the container element (#root). The container is `document.getElementById(\"root\")`. Fine.\n\nBut: React's event delegation for the *root* container uses `container.addEventListener(type, listener)` — but React 19 might use the document as the delegate target for some events... Either way it should work.\n\nHmm, let me consider: maybe the problem is that jsdom's `Event` dispatched via `window.eval` context is a *different realm's* Event? No — `window.Event` is jsdom's Event.\n\nLet me just test a click handler to see if React events work at all in this setup.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794377757645,"end":1794377757666}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794377759979,"sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_EkJOyJWHWTRGH4RMBxfxiTFT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/.run/jsdomtest && cat > debug2.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { JSDOM, VirtualConsole } from \"jsdom\";\n\nconst DIST = \"/workspace/frontend/dist\";\nconst html = fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"index.html\"), \"utf8\");\nconst virtualConsole = new VirtualConsole();\nvirtualConsole.on(\"jsdomError\", (e) => console.log(\"JSDOM ERROR:\", e.message));\nvirtualConsole.on(\"error\", (...args) => console.log(\"console.error:\", ...args));\nconst dom = new JSDOM(html, { runScripts: \"outside-only\", pretendToBeVisual: true, url: \"http://localhost:8000/\", virtualConsole });\nconst { window } = dom;\nwindow.fetch = async () => ({ ok: true, status: 200, text: async () => JSON.stringify({ items: [], total: 0, page: 1, page_size: 10 }) });\nwindow.localStorage.setItem(\"audio-library.token\", \"tok\");\nfor (const file of fs.readdirSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\")).filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".js\"))) {\n  window.eval(fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\", file), \"utf8\"));\n}\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nawait sleep(200);\nconst doc = window.document;\n// click the \"Sign out\" button -> header should switch to guest\nconst signOut = [...doc.querySelectorAll(\"button\")].find((b) => b.textContent.includes(\"Sign out\"));\nconsole.log(\"signout button:\", !!signOut);\nsignOut.dispatchEvent(new window.MouseEvent(\"click\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\nawait sleep(200);\nconsole.log(\"after click:\", doc.body.textContent.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").slice(0, 120));\n// click the tab \"Create account\"\nconst tab = [...doc.querySelectorAll(\"button\")].find((b) => b.textContent.trim() === \"Create account\");\nconsole.log(\"tab:\", !!tab);\nif (tab) {\n  tab.dispatchEvent(new window.MouseEvent(\"click\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\n  await sleep(200);\n  console.log(\"after tab click:\", doc.body.textContent.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").slice(0, 200));\n}\nEOF\ntimeout 120 node debug2.mjs 2>&1 | tail -20"},"output":"signout button: true\nafter click:  Audio LibraryStream tracks stored as linksBrowsing as guestSign inCreate accountWelcome backSign in to add tracks to th\ntab: true\nafter tab click:  Audio LibraryStream tracks stored as linksBrowsing as guestSign inCreate accountCreate your accountRegister to start adding tracks to the library.UsernamePasswordRegisterTracksNo tracks yet.No tracks\n","metadata":{"output":"signout button: true\nafter click:  Audio LibraryStream tracks stored as linksBrowsing as guestSign inCreate accountWelcome backSign in to add tracks to th\ntab: true\nafter tab click:  Audio LibraryStream tracks stored as linksBrowsing as guestSign inCreate accountCreate your accountRegister to start adding tracks to the library.UsernamePasswordRegisterTracksNo tracks yet.No tracks\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/.run/jsdomtest && cat > debug2.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { JSDOM, VirtualConsole } from \"jsdom\";\n\nconst DIST = \"/workspace/frontend/dist\";\nconst html = fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"index.html\"), \"utf8\");\nconst virtualConsole = new VirtualConsole();\nvirtualConsole.on(\"jsdomError\", (e) => console.log(\"JSDOM ERROR:\", e.message));\nvirtualConsole.on(\"error\", (...args) => console.log(\"console.error:\", ...args));\nconst dom = new JSDOM(html, { runScripts: \"outside-only\", pretendToBeVisual: true, url: \"http://localhost:8000/\", virtualConsole });\nconst { window } = dom;\nwindow.fetch = async () => ({ ok: true, status: 200, text: async () => JSON.stringify({ items: [], total: 0, page: 1, page_size: 10 }) });\nwindow.localStorage.setItem(\"audio-library.token\", \"tok\");\nfor (const file of fs.readdirSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\")).filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".js\"))) {\n  window.eval(fs.readFileSync(path.join(DIST, \"assets\", file), \"utf8\"));\n}\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\nawait sleep(200);\nconst doc = window.document;\n// click the \"Sign out\" button -> header should switch to guest\nconst signOut = [...doc.querySelectorAll(\"button\")].find((b) => b.textContent.includes(\"Sign out\"));\nconsole.log(\"signout button:\", !!signOut);\nsignOut.dispatchEvent(new window.MouseEvent(\"click\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\nawait sleep(200);\nconsole.log(\"after click:\", doc.body.textContent.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").slice(0, 120));\n// click the tab \"Create account\"\nconst tab = [...doc.querySelectorAll(\"button\")].find((b) => b.textContent.trim() === \"Create account\");\nconsole.log(\"tab:\", !!tab);\nif (tab) {\n  tab.dispatchEvent(new window.MouseEvent(\"click\", { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));\n  await sleep(200);\n  console.log(\"after tab click:\", doc.body.textContent.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").slice(0, 200));\n}\nEOF\ntimeout 120 node debug2.mjs 2>&1 | tail -20","time":{"start":1794377757656,"end":1794377759961}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c93fb3d00017g1YQSc80xSok2","sessionID":"ses_e36c92cabffe1cdrQ9t4Hp4h3a","messageID":"msg_1c93f85420013uLPE0XXZ30uX1"}}
